    "cex-average-cluster-size-does-not-determine-unequal-size-design-effect": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-cluster-sampling-design-and-cluster-totals",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let the finite element population be partitioned into\nnonempty finite sets\n$$\\mathcal U=\\bigsqcup_{i=1}^{M}U_i,$$\nwhere $M\\ge1$ and $U_i$ is the set of secondary sampling units (SSUs) in the\n$i$th primary sampling unit (PSU).",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-srswor-cluster-total-estimator-unbiased-and-variance",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let a fixed finite population have $M\\ge2$ PSUs with fixed cluster totals\n$T_1,\\ldots,T_M$. Select $m$ PSUs by uniform SRSWOR, where $1\\le m\\le M$.\nFor $S_1$ the selected set, define\n$$\\widehat T_C=\\frac{M}{m}\\sum_{i\\in S_1}T_i,\n\\qquad S_T^2=\\frac1{M-1}\\sum_{i=1}^M(T_i-\\bar T)^2,\n\\qquad \\bar T=\\frac1M\\sum_{i=1}^M T_i.$$\nThen $E_d[\\widehat T_C]=T:=\\sum_{i=1}^M T_i$ and\n$$\\operatorname{Var}_d(\\widehat T_C)\n=\\frac{M^2(1-m/M)}{m}S_T^2.$$",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-moments-variance-and-covariance",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "If $X$ is square-integrable, its **variance** is\n$$\\operatorname{Var}(X):=\\mathbb E[(X-\\mathbb E[X])^2].$$",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-covariance-bilinearity-and-symmetry",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(X_i)_{i\\in I}$ and $(Y_j)_{j\\in J}$ be finite families of square-integrable real random variables on one common probability space. Then covariance is symmetric, and for real scalars $a_i,b_j$,\n$$\\operatorname{Cov}\\!\\left(\\sum_{i\\in I}a_iX_i,\\sum_{j\\in J}b_jY_j\\right)=\\sum_{i\\in I}\\sum_{j\\in J}a_ib_j\\operatorname{Cov}(X_i,Y_j).$$\nThis includes empty sums and constant summands. On a finite probability space all real random variables are square-integrable, so the original finite-space case is included with the same centered-product covariance.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-variance-of-a-finite-sum",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Equivalently, it is\n$\\sum_{i,j\\in I}\\operatorname{Cov}(X_i,X_j)$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Half the PSUs have size 1 and half size 3, so average size is 2; size-3 cluster values share B_i, giving correlation 1 for every existing within-cluster pair and marginal variance σ².",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "A1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "step": "1.2",
          "claim": "For N=2M elements, Var_B(Ȳ_U)=5σ²/(4M), E_B[S_U²]=σ²(2M−5/2)/(2M−1), and the singleton-PSU SRSWOR formula gives the element-sample mean variance.",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "A1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "F4",
            "F5",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "With T_i=n_iB_i and Σn_i²=5M, derive E_B[S_T²]=5σ²; the cluster SRSWOR theorem gives expected cluster-sample mean variance 5σ²(1−k/M)/(4k).",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "A1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "F4",
            "F5",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "Cancel the shared FPC and sample-size factors to obtain (5/2)(2M−1)/(2M−5/2), which is 199/79 at M=100 and tends to 5/2, not the substituted-size prediction 2.",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.1",
            "step 1.2",
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "The counterexample assumes an even M≥4 and k≥1."
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "The model assumes σ²>0; otherwise both variance ratio terms vanish and DEFF is undefined."
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The model includes size-1 PSUs and permits k=1; step 1.1 and the formulas in steps 1.2–2.2 cover these cases."
        },
        {
          "case": "degenerate",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The size-3 PSUs have perfect within-cluster correlation; steps 1.1–3.1 compute the resulting valid model-averaged variance ratio."
        },
        {
          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "The cluster census k=M is excluded; both design variances would be zero and their ratio undefined."
        },
        {
          "case": "nonempty-choice",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Steps 1.1–3.1 use finite sums and finite SRSWOR laws only; no choice axiom is used."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "The size1/size3 construction yields model-averaged ratio(5/2)(2M-1)/(2M-5/2) in Counterexample3.1, refuting arithmetic-average-size substitution. It does not offer a biconditional or a general unequal-cluster DEFF formula. The forward boundary would require a separate asserted biconditional, which this specific claim does not contain."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-reverse",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "The size1/size3 construction yields model-averaged ratio(5/2)(2M-1)/(2M-5/2) in Counterexample3.1, refuting arithmetic-average-size substitution. It does not offer a biconditional or a general unequal-cluster DEFF formula. The reverse boundary would infer these hypotheses or this construction from the conclusion, an implication this specific item does not assert."
        }
      ],
      "finite_checks": [
